
  OPENSWMM ENGINE - VERSION 6.0.0-alpha.2
  -------------------------------------------
  ;;Project Title/Notes
  1D-2D Coupled Weir-Culvert MVP Demo
  100 m (Y) x 1000 m (X) flat plain, longitudinal slope 0.001 toward
  +X. Transverse trapezoidal weir 0.5 m high at X = 500, approximated
  as a triangular ramp at the configured mesh resolution. A 500 m
  circular culvert (50 x 10 m segments, 0.5 m diameter) is buried 1 m
  below the surface along Y = 50 and centered on the weir. Three
  pipe junctions are 2D-coupled: the upstream end J_P00 and the two
  weir-flanking nodes J_P24 / J_P26. The downstream culvert end
  J_P_last drains to a dedicated FREE outfall OUT_CULVERT via a
  short outlet pipe, giving the culvert a clean 1D discharge path.
  Rainfall (SCS Type II 24-hour, 100 mm
  is auto-broadcast to every 2D cell by the engine - no explicit
  SUBCATCHMENTS section needed. The right edge is exposed via 6
  coupled CATCH junctions (one per 20 m of edge, on the mesh) each
  draining through a short outlet pipe to its own offsite OUT_SINK
  outfall
  (the 2D_BOUNDARY_CONDITIONS section documents intent but the
  solver treats all mesh edges as WALL today). 2D state is written to
  weir_culvert.2d.h5 for water-surface and flow-vector animation
  in the GUI.
  
